course: dictionary
lesson: 9897
title: Talc: a soft mineral and a soft powder
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Talc is a mineral, a natural solid found in rocks, and it is very soft. «The Mohs scale ranks minerals from 1 (talc, the softest) to 10 (diamond, the hardest).» Talc is number 1, so it is the softest mineral on the scale.
explain: Use the clues around the word. Softest and hardest are opposites, so talc must sit at the soft end. Talc feels soapy or greasy, and you can scratch it with a fingernail. If you can scratch a rock with your nail, it is very soft.
explain: Talc has a second meaning, talcum powder. This is a fine powder made from talc and put on skin to keep it dry. When a sentence mentions baby, powder or skin, talc means the powder, not the rock. Always check which meaning fits by swapping in your idea.
fact: Talc is a mineral that feels soapy or greasy.
fact: Talc is the softest mineral, number 1 on the Mohs scale.
fact: Diamond is number 10 on the Mohs scale, the hardest mineral.
fact: Talcum powder is a fine powder made from talc, used on skin to keep it dry.
fact: Gymnasts and climbers use talc for grip, so their hands do not slip.
exercise: «The Mohs scale ranks minerals from 1 (talc, the softest) to 10 (diamond, the hardest).» Which mineral is number 1? | *Talc | Diamond | Wood | Granite
exercise: Mum uses talc on the baby's skin. Why? | *To keep the skin dry | To grow hair | To make the skin harder | To make the skin shine
exercise: «The Mohs scale ranks minerals from 1 (talc, the softest) to 10 (diamond, the hardest).» Find and copy the word that means the opposite of hardest. | minerals | scale | *softest | diamond
test: Talc is number 1 on the Mohs scale. What does that tell you about talc? | The heaviest mineral | *The softest mineral | The hardest mineral | The shiniest mineral
test: «Mum dusted talc on the baby to keep her dry.» In this sentence, what is talc? | *A fine powder | A metal tool | A hard rock | A kind of fruit
exam: Which of these is true about talc? | Talc is the hardest mineral, number 10 on the Mohs scale | Talc is a metal that is found in gyms | Talc is used to make diamonds | *Talc is a very soft mineral that feels soapy or greasy
